{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligation 1: node reads build a `Snapshot` from `Domain::node_content` and the content's `NodeContents::fingerprint`, with no further read.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]`\n  - It reads a snapshot through `read_snapshot`, then changes the underlying node contents.\n  - It asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint`, `snapshot.fingerprint.value == \"before\"`, and `snapshot.content.format() == \"before\"` after the change.\n  - It asserts the graph recorded exactly one read (`reads == [1]`), so the snapshot was built without another read.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]`\n  - It runs over an empty string and a large Unicode string.\n  - It asserts `snapshot.fingerprint == fp(original)` and that the content stays unchanged after the graph is replaced.\n  - It asserts the read count is exactly `[1, 1]` for one `read_snapshot` call and one `read` call, so neither call re-read.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]`\n  - It checks that the `read_snapshot` fingerprint equals `fp(\"before\")` and that earlier dependencies keep the old fingerprint after the content changes.\n  - It checks the read counts (`[1, 1, 1, 2]`).\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` check that the snapshot fingerprint is the one recorded as a `Dependency::Node`, and that the read counts match.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks that the content's fingerprint is stable after the source changes and differs after a fresh read.\n\n**Obligation 2: the `Snapshot<T>` shape (`content` and `fingerprint` fields, `new`, `Clone`, `Debug`).**\n- Nothing in the reviewed sources calls `Snapshot::new`, clones a snapshot, or formats one with `Debug`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks only the export inventory.\n- The tests read the public `content` and `fingerprint` fields directly.\n- The implementation, `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]`, is `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` and `#[non_exhaustive]` with the two public fields.\n- The derives and the plain constructor contain no conditionals or transformations, so no behavior here could go wrong without a test noticing. I treat them as covered by the exemption for untested obligations with no logic of their own.\n- I did not read the body of `Snapshot::new`. It is a field-forwarding constructor.\n\n**Delegated obligations.** The fingerprint's own semantics are cited from `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint` and are not reassessed here.\n\nI found no gap, and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
